// A prefab: a piece of a place, drawn as rows of glyphs, and what each glyph
// stands for. The pool stamps it inside an area through `atglyph::mapgen::StampPicks`;
// the engine fills its slots on the arrival that built the place.
//
// Every field:
//   name:   the piece's name, which a pool entry asks for
//   ground: the tile painted under every slot; required when the legend has any
//           slot, and it must be a tile a monster can stand on
//   turn:   optional, Quarter if left out: how far the piece may be turned
//           wherever it is laid: None | Half (as drawn or a half-turn) |
//           Quarter (any quarter-turn)
//   mirror: optional, Both if left out: how it may be mirrored: None |
//           LeftRight | UpDown | Both (either, and both together, the
//           half-turn); the chain that lays it may hold it to fewer facings,
//           never more
//   rows:   the piece, one string per row, all the same width; a space is left as
//           the map had it, and every other glyph must be in the legend
//   legend: glyph to what it stands for, one of
//     Tile("name")                          a tile from assets/tiles.ron
//     Prop("name")                          a prop from props.ron
//     Item(item: "item", count: 1)          that item, by name; count is 1 or
//                                           a range, count: (fewest, most)
//     Item(tag: "tag", count: 1, band: 0)   drawn by tag at the place's band
//                                           plus band
//     Monster(monster: "monster")           that monster
//     Monster(role: "role", band: 0)        drawn for a role
//     Mark                                  a position the game finds by this
//                                           glyph and fills itself: in a risk-and-
//                                           reward or reward piece, 'z' a sleeper
//                                           of the floor's own, 'Z' an ogre asleep,
//                                           'G' a goblin asleep, 'C' a captive of
//                                           the floor's own, shackled, and 'c' a
//                                           cell of a sunken causeway, hidden as
//                                           the deep water round it until it is
//                                           spotted (`src/vaults.rs`)
//     Entry                                 a cell of a grown piece's outer wall
//                                           where it may be joined; a piece grown
//                                           in `hall wall` and `hall floor` is
//                                           walled and floored as its floor is
//
// A chest of things two floors deeper than the room it stands in, in a room
// walled in behind a secret door: the pool's `prefer: Hidden` puts it there,
// and `dungeon.rs` hides a room for it on every floor that draws it.
(
    name: "Hidden Cache",
    ground: "hall floor",
    turn: Quarter,
    mirror: Both,
    rows: [
        "h",
    ],
    legend: {
        'h': Prop("cache chest"),
    },
)
